  "notes": "v269 — AUTH-LOGOUT-ON-UPDATE (owner, Mon Oct 26, 2026 13:22 MDT, screen recording: cold start -> splash Checking for updates -> Downloading -> Update ready, restarting -> lands on the Sign Up / Sign In landing, fully signed out; the same morning's five OTA relaunches each forced a sign-in). PROVEN MECHANISM: the session was IGNORED at boot, never destroyed. js/ota.js gates App.init on OTA.ready() (hosted version.json fetch in the bundled copy; serial Filesystem re-verification of every bundle file in the downloaded copy — the slowest thing at boot); js/firebase.js inits ungated at DOMContentLoaded and its first onAuthStateChanged restores the persisted user (SDK default LOCAL persistence at origin https://localhost — OTA.restart() only navigates via Capacitor.convertFileSrc to the /_capacitor_file_/ PATH on that same origin, so the store is shared across bundle swaps). The restore lands BEFORE init; init's onboarded branch then called App.onAuth(null) UNCONDITIONALLY, slamming the v216 lock over the restored session, and that branch has no re-check — the landing stuck until a manual form sign-in. FIX (web only): js/firebase.js gains the first-verdict channel (FB.authStateKnown / FB.authUnavailable / FB.whenAuthKnown(); SDK-missing/init-failure mark known-null + authUnavailable); js/app.js init routes on App.bootAuthMode (user/null/wait/legacy) — while wait, the splash HOLDS with no view routed and the verdict (or a 15 s wedged-restore fallback) routes; legacy (pre-v269 firebase.js, harness stubs) is the pre-v269 behaviour byte-for-byte. Explicit sign-out untouched. New suite tools/auth-gate-v269-test.js 52/52 (red pre-fix: W1 reproduced the incident exactly). A/B zero regressions (signin-lock 92/0, pullgate 31/0, ingest 217/0, edit-start 28/0, cloudsync 51/0+14/0 identical). ON-PHONE PROOF: the restart INTO v269 still boots the old bundle — the fix proves on the NEXT update restart (v270+) or any cold start on the v269 bundle: splash -> update -> restarting -> dashboard STILL SIGNED IN.",
